@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 45

component "Godot 4.7.2\nproject.godot\nCompatibility; movement + hero InputMap" as Godot
component "Main / pixel_viewport.gd\nInteger-scaled SubViewportContainer\nExpands logical view on resize" as Main
component "MovementGame\nInput, fixture controls, chat, HUD\nCentered Camera2D" as Game
component "GridView\nDraws tiles and existing sprites" as View
component "GridWorld + GridActor\nBlocking, movement credit\nOrdered wandering / pursuit / combat" as World
component "HeroState + HeroData + SkillRank\nMage baseline, XP, learned ranks" as Hero
component "MeleeRules + MeleeProfile + SwingTimer\nSourced physical outcomes / timing" as Combat
component "CombatPanel\nInteraction / swing boundaries / death" as CombatUI
component "HeroPanel\nCharacter / spell book modal" as Panel
component "MovementFixture\nFixed grounds and seeded wanderers" as Fixture
component "GUT 9.7.1\ntest/unit/" as Tests
component "Validation\ntools/validate.ps1" as Validation
artifact "reports/\nLogs, JSON, JUnit XML, diagrams" as Reports

Godot --> Main : loads
Main --> Game : contains in SubViewport
Game --> Fixture : reset / startup
Fixture --> World : constructs
Game --> World : move / wait / cast / melee
World --> Combat : resolves attacks
Game --> CombatUI : opens / refreshes
CombatUI --> World : select / interact / continue
CombatUI --> Game : action / selection / reset
World --> Hero : owns; applies XP
Game --> Panel : opens / refreshes
Panel --> Game : cast requested
Panel --> Hero : reads
World --> Game : chat message
Game --> View : refresh after action
View --> World : reads tiles and actors
Validation --> Godot : imports, parses, starts
Validation --> Tests : full suite
Tests --> Game : input, camera, UI
Tests --> World : movement and ordering
Validation --> Reports : checks results; renders diagrams

note bottom of World
Milestones 1–3: movement, hero, melee, pursuit, interaction, death overlay.
Real spells, equipment/loot, and Loop lifecycle follow later.
end note
@enduml
